ro showdown value and zero potential to improve significantly on the river unless I miraculously hit a runner-runner straight which is impossible now as only one card is left.\nActually, let's look at the straight again.\nI have 6, 7. Board has 8. I need 9 and 10 for a straight. One card to come. Impossible to make a straight.\nI have 6, 7. Board has 8. I need 5, 4. Impossible to make a straight with one card.\nI have effectively 0% equity to make a straight.\nI have no flush draw.\nI have bottom pair outs (hitting a 6 or 7) which would likely still lose to J, K, or A pairs.\n\nThe opponent checked the Flop and Pre-flop. They might be trapping or also have nothing (low pocket pair, unmatched low cards). However, A, K, J hits almost every reasonable range.\nSince I am in the lead cumulatively and start with fresh stacks, preservation of capital is fine, but checking is free.\nMy valid actions include Check (0).\nChecking allows me to see the River for free. If the opponent bets the River, I fold. If they check, I lose at showdown, but I lose the minimum.\nBluffing here is risky because the board hits the opponent's range too well (A, K, J).\n\nReason:\nI have no made hand and no draws. The board (A, K, J, 8) connects very well with most hands an opponent would have. Although the opponent has shown passivity by checking, bluffing into a board that favors their range so heavily is dangerous. Checking is the safest option to minimize loss.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
