e river card for free, maximizing my chances to win the pot. I will choose to check (0).\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The current hand is Ace-high (A, Q, 6, 5, 4) with a gutshot straight draw (holding 4, board has 2-5-6, needing a 3). The opponent has shown passivity by checking on the Pre-flop, Flop, and Turn. While Ace-high has some showdown value, it is vulnerable. Betting might fold out hands with equity, but getting check-raised would be disastrous.\n\nReason: Checking is the most prudent play here. It allows you to see the River card for free, giving you a chance to hit your straight (a 3) or pair your Ace without investing more chips. Since you are leading the overall match, avoiding unnecessary variance in a small pot with a marginal hand preserves your advantage.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
